Chewy, golden bar cookies rich with notes of brown butter and molasses caramel, studded with bittersweet chocolate chips and crunchy roasted peanuts. The combination of bittersweet chocolate and savory salted nuts gives these blondies a sophisticated sweet-and-salty balance.

*Adapted from [Epicurious](http://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/chocolate-chip-and-peanut-blondies-353839).*

## Ingredients

- 1 cup all-purpose flour
- ½ teaspoon salt
- ¼ teaspoon baking soda
- ½ cup (1 stick) unsalted butter
- 1 ¼ cups packed light brown sugar (or golden brown sugar)
- 2 large eggs, room temperature
- 1 teaspoon pure vanilla extract
- ½ cup salted roasted peanuts, coarsely chopped and divided
- ½ cup bittersweet chocolate chips (approx. 3 oz), divided

## Instructions

1. **Preheat and Prepare Pan:** Heat oven to 350°F (175°C). Lightly grease an 8x8-inch metal baking pan and dust with flour, or line with parchment paper leaving a small overhang on opposite sides for easy removal later.
2. **Combine Dry Goods:** In a medium bowl, whisk together the all-purpose flour, salt, and baking soda until uniform. Set aside.
3. **Melt Butter and Blend Sugar:** In a medium heavy-bottomed saucepan, melt the butter over low heat. Pull the pan off the burner, dump in the brown sugar, and whisk vigorously until the mixture is uniform and silky. Let rest off the heat for 2 to 3 minutes so it cools slightly before the eggs are added.
4. **Beat in Eggs and Vanilla:** Whisk in the room-temperature eggs one at a time, followed by the vanilla extract. Whisk steadily until the batter appears glossy and emulsified.
5. **Gently Fold Batter:** Switch to a flexible rubber or silicone spatula and stir in the flour mixture just until dry pockets vanish. Gently fold in half of the chopped peanuts and half of the bittersweet chocolate chips.
6. **Layer and Garnish:** Scrape the thick batter into the prepared baking pan, smoothing it into corners with your spatula. Scatter the remaining peanuts and chocolate chips evenly over the surface.
7. **Bake to Golden Perfection:** Bake on the middle oven rack for 28 to 32 minutes. The blondies are done when the surface turns rich golden brown, edges just start to pull away from the pan sides, and a cake tester inserted in the center comes out clean or with moist crumbs (no wet batter).
8. **Cool and Slice:** Transfer the pan to a wire cooling rack and let cool completely. Once fully cooled, lift out using the parchment sling and slice into 16 squares.

## Notes

- **Make Ahead:** Store cooled blondie squares in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 3 to 4 days, separated by parchment sheets.
- **Metal vs. Glass Pan:** Metal pans bake blondies and brownies with sharper, crisper edges and even centers. If using a glass dish, reduce oven temperature by 25°F (to 325°F) and check for doneness around 32–35 minutes.
